Package: potatrip
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: N5SKT <dweeks@localhost>
Installed-Size: 2000
Depends: python3, python3-venv, python3-pip, systemd, logrotate
Section: hamradio
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/dlweeks/PotaTrip
Description: POTA Trip Planner - Parks on the Air trip planning web app
 Plans multi-park POTA activation trips from a city: filters the POTA park
 database by radius, trip-hours and trip-miles, builds a greedy multi-park
 route that fits the budget (including the drive home), and returns a
 Google Maps directions URL with the parks as ordered waypoints. Includes
 a Road Trip tab for point-to-point driving trips with parks along the route.
 .
 The app is installed under /opt/PotaTrip. The python3 virtual environment
 (.venv) is built ON THE TARGET at install time with the system python3,
 so no pre-built binaries ship in the package and it works on any
 architecture (amd64, arm64 / Raspberry Pi). Launched via
 /usr/local/bin/potatrip as the systemd service "potatrip" on port 5001.
